<LegalPage title="Security Policy - Doer" description="Report security issues in Doer and protect your local host." heading="Doer Security Policy" lede="Doer runs tools on your computer. Report suspected vulnerabilities privately and protect access to your host and connected providers." effectiveDate="2026-10-07" lastUpdated="2026-10-07" sections={sections}>
  <section id="reporting"><h2>Reporting issues</h2><p>Send suspected Doer vulnerabilities to <a href="mailto:aryan@lagaryan.click">aryan@lagaryan.click</a>. Include the affected version, operating system, reproduction steps and likely impact. Remove passwords, tokens and personal task contents from evidence. Do not publish exploitation details before we have had an opportunity to investigate.</p><p>Research only on systems and data you own or have permission to test. Do not access other users' data, interrupt their service or test third-party providers without their authorization. This policy does not grant permission to access systems or waive applicable laws.</p></section>
  <section id="use"><h2>Protecting your computer</h2><p>Doer runs a local backend, reads and writes selected folders and starts provider command-line tools. Review task instructions and consequential actions, keep backups and use provider permissions appropriate for your work. Protect API keys and connected accounts. Only pair devices you trust, keep pairing links private and revoke access when a device is no longer trusted.</p><p>Keep your operating system, Doer and provider tools updated. Store builds receive updates through Microsoft Store; direct downloads use the project's release channel. Do not expose a local server publicly without an appropriately secured network configuration. No software or storage method is completely secure.</p></section>
  <section id="contact"><h2>Contact and updates</h2><p>Doer is operated by Aryan Gupta and Aditya Mayank Sinha. T3 Tools, Inc. is the upstream MIT copyright holder, not the operator. Security and support contact: <a href="mailto:aryan@lagaryan.click">aryan@lagaryan.click</a>. We will revise this page as reporting guidance changes.</p></section>
</LegalPage>
